{
  "_comment": [
    "The CWOps \"CW 77\" list (#240), pinned for both ports: MorseData.cw77 in",
    "ios/Sources/MorseKit/MorseDataCW77.swift and android/.../morsekit/MorseDataCW77.kt.",
    "Read by ios/Sources/MorseKitCheck/main.swift and",
    "android/app/src/test/.../morsekit/MorseDataCW77Test.kt.",
    "",
    "`source` is the maintainer-supplied file 77_all_current.txt exactly as",
    "sent: 75 whitespace-separated entries in 15 rows of 5, reading order. It",
    "is the authoritative list (no separate CWOps URL exists, per #240).",
    "RR, CL, WX, BEAM and AR each appear twice; the set is `source` with",
    "repeats dropped, keeping the first occurrence: 70 items, in `items`.",
    "The name stays \"CW 77\" although the count differs.",
    "",
    "Token spelling follows fixtures/qso-elements.json: the five entries in",
    "`prosigns` are sent run-together, so their token is the bracketed name",
    "MorseData.prosigns already uses (<AR>, <AS>, <BT>, <KN>, <SK>); every",
    "other entry is sent as text, including BK and CL (the abbreviations",
    "table's letter forms, \"break\" and \"closing down\") and K (a letter",
    "whose pattern is the <K> prosign's anyway). HW? keeps its question mark.",
    "Meanings repeat the wording of MorseData.abbreviations, qCodes, prosigns",
    "and qsoElements wherever the token already lives there; the tests check.",
    "",
    "`personal` pins the \"include my callsign and name\" rule. The callsign",
    "is the app's existing Your callsign setting, the name the Your name",
    "setting beside it. Each is trimmed and uppercased and loses every",
    "character with no Morse pattern (MorseCode.pattern); a name keeps one",
    "space between its words. A callsign that is empty, or is the",
    "placeholder default `placeholderCallsign`, counts as unset; an empty",
    "name counts as unset. The callsign comes first, then the name, appended",
    "after the 70; either is dropped if it is already a CW 77 token or equals",
    "the one before it. The switch is offered only when the rule yields at",
    "least one token. Expected values were worked by hand from the rule.",
    "",
    "`recommended` is the playback Bob Carter WR7Q recommends for this list:",
    "40 WPM, Farnsworth off. The apps offer it as a one-tap preset."
  ],
